From: Pedro Baltazar <pedrobtz@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH P8] ggml : do not define static_assert as a macro in C23

Upstream pull request: (not opened yet; see design §9.3)

In C23 static_assert is a keyword, so the fallback macro in
ggml-common.h and ggml-impl.h is not needed, and defining it hides the
keyword: clang 22 and 23 warn "keyword is hidden by macro definition
[-Wkeyword-macro]" when C is compiled as -std=gnu23, which R's
r-devel-linux-x86_64-debian-clang check flavour does. Skip the macro
when __STDC_VERSION__ is C23 or later.

--- a/src/ggml-common.h
+++ b/src/ggml-common.h
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
 #if defined(GGML_COMMON_DECL)
 
 #ifndef __cplusplus
-#ifndef static_assert
+#if !defined(static_assert) && !(defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 202311L)
 #if defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && (__STDC_VERSION__ >= 201100L)
 #define static_assert(cond, msg) _Static_assert(cond, msg)
 #else
--- a/src/ggml-impl.h
+++ b/src/ggml-impl.h
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 // if C99 - static_assert is noop
 // ref: https://stackoverflow.com/a/53923785/4039976
 #ifndef __cplusplus
-    #ifndef static_assert
+    #if !defined(static_assert) && !(defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && __STDC_VERSION__ >= 202311L)
         #if defined(__STDC_VERSION__) && (__STDC_VERSION__ >= 201100L)
             #define static_assert(cond, msg) _Static_assert(cond, msg)
         #else
